course: dictionary
lesson: 9010
title: Skimming
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Skimming means reading quickly to get the general idea of a text, without reading every word. «Skimming means reading quickly to get the general idea of a text.» Your eyes move fast over the headings, the first lines and the key words.
explain: Think of a stone skimming across a lake. It touches the top of the water, moves fast and barely dips in. A skimmer reads the top of the page the same way, moving quickly and not stopping on every detail.
explain: Skimming is different from reading slowly to learn every detail. It is also different from scanning, which hunts for one fact, such as a date or a name. Skimming finds the big idea first, and you can read the details later if you need them.
fact: Skimming means reading quickly to get the main idea, without reading every word.
fact: Skimming also means removing something from the top of a liquid, like cream from milk or fat from soup.
fact: Skimming stones means throwing flat stones so they bounce across water; in the USA this is often called «skipping stones».
fact: Skimming can also mean moving quickly just above a surface, like a bird skimming the water.
fact: Card skimming is secretly copying bank card details with a hidden device, so grown-ups cover the keypad and check the card slot on cash machines.
exercise: «Skimming means reading quickly to get the general idea of a text.» What does skimming mean when you read? | Reading every word very slowly | Copying a text word for word | Reading out loud to a friend | *Reading quickly to get the main idea
exercise: Maya is skimming the soup to take off the fat from the top. What does skimming mean here? | Adding salt to the soup | Stirring the soup very fast | *Removing something from the top of a liquid | Pouring the soup into a bowl
exercise: Which reading skill helps you find one date in a long text quickly? | Skimming, to get the main idea | *Scanning, to find one fact | Reading every word twice | Skimming stones on a lake
test: Which sentence uses skimming to mean moving just above a surface? | The tired boy read every line slowly | She added salt to the stew | *A swallow was skimming over the pond | He copied the words into his book
test: Skimming stones means throwing flat stones so that they do what on water? | Turn into mud | *Bounce across the surface | Sink straight down | Freeze into ice
exam: Which is the best way to use skimming when you have ten minutes to find the main idea of a long article? | Skip the article and guess | *Read quickly, looking at headings and first sentences | Read only the last sentence and stop | Read every word slowly, from start to finish
